<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad II of Znojmo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1161">1161</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/znojmo">Znojmo</a> was a Přemyslid prince who ruled the Moravian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of Znojmo in the 12th century. He led the Moravian princes who challenged Duke Vladislaus II for the Bohemian throne, besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> in 1142. Defeated after Vladislaus obtained help from King Conrad III, he later reconciled with the duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-ii-of-znojmo.jpg" alt="Conrad II of Znojmo" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous fresco in Znojmo (CZ) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konrad_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
